{"title":"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> and right triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8451bee5a68657a8f8d5c57de669c2de023c04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DCE$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> have the same area. They are joined to form a trapezoid, as shown. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/5/c358884777664e69762bbb69b74c260349626ff4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(250); defaultpen(linewidth(0.8)); pair A=(0,5),B=origin,C=(6,0),D=(6,5),E=(18,0); draw(A--B--E--D--cycle^^C--D); draw(rightanglemark(D,C,E,30)); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,NW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SW); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,S); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,N); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,S); label(&quot;$5$&quot;,A/2,W); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,(A+D)/2,N); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"152\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/0/9d09d9bac91d9168585d9aa99369ddd789d07abf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }12\\qquad\\textbf{(B) }13\\qquad\\textbf{(C) }14\\qquad\\textbf{(D) }15\\qquad\\textbf{(E) }16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b9e3b4859c5a49ea66f0add510fa64a7f02bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup CDE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/09675631121b100ad3a004a2881ff8600fcf773a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{DC\\cdot CE}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"74\" height=\"37\" />. The area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/6/9964faa5242fdba498eb342b2824a6f6156e3071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\cdot AD=5\\cdot 6=30$\" width=\"168\" height=\"13\" />, which also must be equal to the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b9e3b4859c5a49ea66f0add510fa64a7f02bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup CDE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, which, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f94985206e7b5c025804fd9e07856a32512e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />, must in turn equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/a/63a133b666eb488c86a0b15679d69705cd9bde17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\cdot CE}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"53\" height=\"37\" />. Through transitivity, then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/3/d7340acea50cbf60b6ca221f99f495a12ce7695a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5\\cdot CE}{2}=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"37\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/e/2fedb75fb84abe069e24a618a61411024b06b50c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE=12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />. Then, using the Pythagorean Theorem, you should be able to figure out that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/b/f8b9e3b4859c5a49ea66f0add510fa64a7f02bd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\bigtriangleup CDE$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> triangle, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/7/f9717fe5342bdb614c826705e4e6bb56dd9e1c62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE=\\boxed{13}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"84\" height=\"23\" /> , or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the rectangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/c/a6c9ac8c3722d5ef6c3c9cdbca6aac6ab27bacd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5\\times6=30.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"90\" height=\"15\" /> Since the parallel line pairs are identical, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/f/77f94985206e7b5c025804fd9e07856a32512e6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC=5$\" width=\"62\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a28663142cb9f74e4155fc8b9097345372b285e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{5x}{2}=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" /> is the area of the right triangle. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/8/568f0e013159ff1f70ab294613eb37bdc4fba105.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=12.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> According to the Pythagorean Theorem, we have a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/6/c1645fea006e40422df8465ad25c74bc33e615eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5-12-13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> triangle. So, the hypotenuse <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> has to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>This problem can be solved with the Pythagorean Theorem (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/b/7fbd4264fbec874b1c14992abd59ea22d4daf604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2 + b^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"16\" />).  We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/d/01d5e32c1ab994001b016f6b2070fb9b1e59461b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = DC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/c/edc75b686340a97d000059a44d94b95951c533fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DC = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13c970cbf5e2e7029089517d5e8efbb8cade6d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> is twice the length of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/1/3d10ce6b774a162708b3107aa0da533c8088a69d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CE = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/c/30c356ee8af95fe3fcd00352e8cd88ba79720fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2 + 12^2 = c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/3/3b31bdf57c202bda35b77d630124399deab12b96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5^2 = 25$\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/4/47466edb148dcae3a1ab096cdaea4f2aed4589d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12^2 = 144$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"77\" height=\"15\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/1/d81e8c94851e105c91977852b314fa9b86c3dff7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 + 144 = 169$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/2/3629b1f1f3b22f1a3c927c7ac0467574394f17ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$169$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> has a square root of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the hypotenuse or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/0/030e19e4e2f1c074127cb50581e8496470c5419f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p><p>——MiracleMaths\n</p><p>Note: Another way to find out that CE is 12 is by using logic. Since DC = 5, we can reason that the triangle is a 5 - 12 - 13 triangle, because the only Pythagorean Triple with 5 as a leg(not hypotenuse, as that would be the case for a 3 - 4 - 5 right triangle), is 5 - 12 - 13. We know DE is the hypotenuse, so it can’t be 12, which means CE has to be 12, which, in turn, means that DE has to be: 13 <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/ToM-f4WMWjQ\">https://youtu.be/ToM-f4WMWjQ</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-JsXX8WLASg\">https://youtu.be/-JsXX8WLASg</a> ~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=88\">https://youtu.be/j3QSD5eDpzU?t=88</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8\" title=\"2014 AMC 8\">2014 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2014\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2014_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2014 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" 